  "body": "## Change and mathematical scope\n\nIndependently certify the fixed PR2575 owner evacuation against PR2530, and prove the exact range where it lowers the recursive rank bill. Both 281,052-role allocations pass the literal window, width, family and slice constraints. The evacuation moves 547 whole-helper occurrences between bins, changes 694 role descriptors and 462 residual ranks, preserves rank mass, and adds 56 positive-rank children.\n\nFor `F(p) = sum_r (H2575[r]-H2530[r])*r^p`, there is exactly one zero in `0<p<1`, with `0.289994 < p_* < 0.289995`. The new rank bill is strictly lower for `p_*<p<1`, and strictly higher below `p_*`. The initial all-exponent-dominance question is therefore answered negatively; the useful completed result is the exact crossover classification. This does not identify an error in PR2575's stated endpoint.\n\nThe proof uses the signed hinge function `sum d_r min(r,t)`, its single sign change at `57/29`, and a strictly decreasing normalized integral. Rational logarithm/Taylor enclosures certify the bracket signs. No floating-point sign decision or approximate root is an acceptance condition.\n\nOnly `research/t74-evacuation-power-audit/` is added. This is a finite allocation certificate and scoped analytic proof. No new supplier, endpoint, \u03ba, optimizer minimum, selected-frontier change or full multiplication theorem is claimed. Native dirty-state/phase replay, physical chart realization, complete movement/precision charges and outer admission remain inherited and unchecked here.\n\n## Task and overlap\n\nThe claim is in [discussion #2616](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/discussions/2616). Main was fetched at entry and again at 2026-10-15 16:29:41 UTC, and remained `0fdd7d82de03e43c9e5a1000dfbcd380d1b687d2`, priority revision 4. The two dependency heads also remained unchanged:\n\n- PR2530, @zxv: `b4012098048e12500b2d33d2e84be281915a27ac`.\n- PR2575, @jeremykothe2: `921c229b4f030121a1d305de6259e174cd391955`.\n\nPriority revision 5 (main `b4560d9e7216f72b73c5aa940ac099c05e33ccf9`, 2026-10-15 16:31:36 UTC) landed after that check. It changes guidance documents only and leaves the `independent-moment` card, both heads above and this package's base-commit pins unchanged.\n\nThe source index pins all 19 retained files by exact upstream path, commit, Git blob and SHA256. Both complete BORROW-WORD JSON objects agree between the sources, as do order and dispatch. Helper endpoint dimensions are independently derived from complete GF(2)^9 vector sets. Local paid profiles are source-reported common quantities; their internal frame invoice is not independently rederived here and cancels in the comparison.\n\nTask card:\n\n- **Task ID / scope key:** `independent-moment`; `PR2575-vs-PR2530/actual-owner-evacuation/single-power-crossover/complete-map-legality`. Recorded card retrieval nonce `59eb0b25697209d2f3021d0193fc238a`, catalogue key `c6f2494b197df3bc3591`.\n- **Base and exact predecessors:** the main and two heads above; PR2559 is the credited evacuation-method predecessor, not an executed dependency.\n- **Concrete object and question:** the two fixed whole-helper maps, their actual chronological legality and their rank power-sum difference for all real `0<p<1`.\n- **Scope status:** refined. A live central dirty-borrowing record supplies a specific independent-audit target. The initial uniform-dominance hypothesis fails; the same-object crossover classification completes the audit.\n- **Exact claim audited:** PR2575's allocation and claimed rank-cost improvement; the added all-exponent question is ours, not a claim attributed to PR2575.\n- **Method and bounded domain:** all 666 calls, all 281,052 roles per map, all 149,184 bins per map; integer event positions/occupancy, exact endpoint subspaces, rational enclosures and an analytic integral argument. No alternative-fill search.\n- **Nearest overlap:** PR2530 constructs the words/fill; PR2575 constructs and already checks the evacuation; PR2559 supplies the method. Discussion #2606 audits lender values; Discussion #2605/PR2588 audits changed local labels; Discussion #2608/PR2571 seeks a chronology lower bound. Discussion #2612 searches new assignments. None is this fixed-map crossover comparison. Existing allocation checks are explicitly corroboration.\n- **Cost budget / observable result:** include every changed idle residual, bind common words and dispatch, and identify the sign of the complete recursive rank-cost delta. Unexamined movement/precision/outer charges are not assumed equal.\n- **Evidence / stop test / cap:** finite receipt, full proof, nine semantic controls, four integrity controls; bounded 60-minute session, no full supplier or new-record construction.\n- **Credit / artifact / reproduction:** credited below; package README, RESULT and source index; `python3 -I -B scripts/research_package.py --package research/t74-evacuation-power-audit`.\n\nFinal cached overlap covered 812 open PRs (2026-10-15 16:22:35 UTC), 1,276 Discussion records (16:27:10 UTC), and the older 799-PR changed-path index (15:59:04 UTC), with complete reported pagination. Offline freshness warnings and truncated PR file lists remain explicit in `OVERLAP.json`; these checks are not a novelty certificate. Exact relevant heads were fetched separately.\n\n## Validation\n\nPassed on CPython 3.12.3 / Linux x86_64, standard library only:\n\n```sh\npython3 -I -B scripts/research_package.py --package research/t74-evacuation-power-audit\npython3 -I -O -B research/t74-evacuation-power-audit/verify.py\npython3 -I -B scripts/research_package.py --package research/t74-evacuation-power-audit --check-only\n```\n\nExpected primary output:\n\n```text\nPASS_T74_EVACUATION_POWER_AUDIT roles_per_map=281052 changed_bins=462 crossover=(0.289994,0.289995) controls=9\n```\n\nThe primary replay reconstructs all 1,332 physical windows from 2,220 per-replica events, including 666 bridges, and checks all eleven emitted owner fields. Nine controls reject missing/ill-typed roles, invalid offsets/windows, family aliasing, overlapping slices, prefix holes, reversed cost direction and lost rank mass. Reversed row order preserves the result; independent integer square roots corroborate the interval evaluator.\n\nThe registered integrity check passes source-byte mutation, JSON value-type mutation, exclusive-output refusal and a Git-free read-only export, with all exported bytes unchanged. All 19 vendored files were also compared directly with their exact upstream Git objects. Metadata/source pins and staged whitespace checks pass. Ordinary replay writes no tracked files; receipt regeneration refuses existing outputs.\n\nNot run: the predecessor's full native/supplier/outer cold replay, physical Clifford/projector checks, full precision/stock/bit-side admission, Lean, hosted CI or independent human review. The proof is a written analytic argument with exact finite hypotheses, not a proof-assistant theorem.\n\n## Credit\n\nJeremy Kothe (@jeremykothe2), PR2575, produced the evacuated fill. Philippe Van Velzen (@philippeVV), PR2559, introduced evacuation. @zxv, PR2530, supplied the eight source-partner aliases, both words, the diagonal order and starting allocation. Cinna Davis (@1337isnot1337), PR2226, introduced anticipatory dirty borrowing; Tekalign (@tekuuu), PR2436, Vlado Vojdanovski, PR2322, and the retained T74/native/controller lineage remain credited. Existing allocation checks and the elementary integral/sign-change method are not claimed as new inventions. Source notices and Apache-2.0 licensing are retained.\n\nPrepared for commdata2338 (@commdata2338), with substantial OpenAI Codex assistance.\n\n**AI assistance:** submitted by @commdata2338 with substantial AI assistance. OpenAI Codex (GPT-6 Astra) did the derivation, the implementation, the checking and the writing; it was packaged and submitted with Claude Code. No independent human review is claimed.\n\n## Open next questions\n\nThe README and TASK.json identify two bounded follow-ups: test one legal same-word evacuation whose signed hinge function is nonpositive at every knot, or compare an existing alternative spectrum while keeping words and order exactly fixed. These would distinguish uniform concave-cost dominance from optimization at one exponent. Both need an actual legal replacement and source-bound allocation checks before any full supplier or \u03ba claim.\n\n## Workflow feedback (optional)\n\nThe overlap helper, exclusive handoff reservation and source-word equality checks made a distinct central audit feasible. A short machine-readable list of changed owner bins and explicitly intended exponent range would make evacuation submissions easier to compare. This is optional supporting evidence, not a proposed new admission requirement.\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01X86sCSXdoDd61SDFfC1PKG\n",
